# Accepted vulnerability findings, with a reason and a review date.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE, and the format below is the point of the file.
#
# The scan gate in .github/workflows/build-sign.yml fails only on findings that
# have a FIX AVAILABLE. That removes the usual reason this file fills up with
# undated entries — an unfixed CVE in a base image does not need suppressing
# because it was never gating.
#
# When a fixable finding genuinely cannot be fixed yet, it belongs here WITH a
# reason and a date, in this shape:
#
#   # CVE-2025-00000 — urllib3. Fix needs httpx 0.29, which drops the API used
#   # in web/main.py. Not reachable: the endpoint does not parse redirects.
#   # Accepted 2026-10-20, review by 2026-11-20.
#   CVE-2025-00000
#
# A bare CVE id on its own line silences the finding permanently and tells the
# next reader nothing about whether it still applies. That is how a scanner
# stops being useful.
